      "id": "COR-CTX-001",
      "impact": "At local time 7000001.5 a G write is accepted with observer admission expired at 7000001.0; at 7000002.5 it is accepted with context lease expired at 7000002.0. All three admissions remain cached. The native Linux expiry check still provides a separate last defense for the lease case; this finding does not claim that native expiry was bypassed or that an experiment passed.",
      "minimal_correction": "After every readiness poll (including oracle.require_ready), perform a final non-polling check of own, peer and oracle admission expiries plus ContextLease.check immediately before the write. Keep native expiry enforcement. On rejection, invalidate the affected cached admissions. Add both shorter-peer and shorter-lease regressions at the final oracle poll.",
      "priority": "blocker",
      "reproduction": {
        "command": "PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B -W error::ResourceWarning independent_probes_v2.py (in a fresh private output copy; do not overwrite retained outputs)",
        "expected": "Reject before writing G; invalidate stale admissions, rather than transition to START_DISPATCHED.",
        "function": "expiry_during_final_oracle_poll",
        "method": "Use real ContextSource/ContextLease acquisition with synthetic kernel reader and Docker metadata, production OracleSession.require_ready and ProcessStream._send, and an intercepted os.write. Advance the shared fake monotonic clock only during the second oracle poll (the final before_write guard). No subprocess or native execution.",
